# Per-developer local overrides for the web app — copy to `.env.local` in
# this same directory (`apps/web/.env.local`). Next.js loads it
# automatically for `next dev`, and it is git-ignored, so nothing here ever
# gets committed.
#
# Why this file exists, not just the shared root `.env`: every
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variable gets baked into the browser bundle at build/dev
# start. The monorepo's root `.env` is shared with every other service —
# including, on a machine also used for real operations, values that
# legitimately point at a real deployment. Running `next dev` after
# sourcing that file silently sends local browser traffic at a real API
# (this happened once already — see `src/lib/runtime-config.ts`). Put your
# personal local overrides here instead, and you never need to touch the
# root `.env` for frontend work at all.
#
# You do not need to set anything below to run `pnpm dev` — every default
# already points at localhost. Uncomment only what you actually need to
# change.

# The API this frontend calls. Defaults to http://localhost:3001 when unset
# in development — only set this if your API runs somewhere else (a
# different port, a container's LAN IP for testing from a phone, etc.).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WITNESS_API_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Required in addition to the above ONLY if that URL is not local
# (loopback, a private 10.x/172.16-31.x/192.168.x address, or *.local) —
# resolveApiBaseUrl() refuses a non-local API URL in development otherwise.
# Acknowledging this here, in your own gitignored file, is the point: it
# can never end up being someone else's default.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WITNESS_ALLOW_REMOTE_DEV_API=true

# Cosmetic — which banner the app shell shows. Leave as development locally.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WITNESS_PROFILE=development
